{"ts": 0.037479, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[3J\u001b[H\u001b[2J", "len": 11}
{"ts": 0.03917, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m──\u001b[0m \u001b[93mshelltutor\u001b[0m \u001b[90m──\u001b[0m \u001b[90mModule · shells\u001b[0m \u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m \u001b[90m──\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 239}
{"ts": 0.039261, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mshells: what runs your commands\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nThree short lessons, then a task. This module stands alone and saves\r\nnothing. You'll look at the shell as a program, at other shells, and\r\nat the difference between your login shell and this one.\r\n\r\nAssumes the five stages, or that you know \u001b[92mls\u001b[0m, \u001b[92mcd\u001b[0m and \u001b[92m>\u001b[0m.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m for lesson 1.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 382}
{"ts": 0.042888, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mnext\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(go on)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(this screen again)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mprev\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(back)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(save and leave)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 159}
{"ts": 0.04317, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 253}
{"ts": 0.058147, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[?2004hshelltutor> ", "len": 20}
{"ts": 0.058268, "dir": "in", "enc": "utf8", "data": "next\n", "len": 5}
{"ts": 0.058303, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "next\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r", "len": 15}
{"ts": 0.063689, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[3J\u001b[H\u001b[2J", "len": 11}
{"ts": 0.065202, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[90m──\u001b[0m \u001b[90mModule\u001b[0m \u001b[90m───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m \u001b[93mshells  1/3\u001b[0m \u001b[90m──\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 245}
{"ts": 0.065278, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\r\n", "len": 2}
{"ts": 0.065312, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;97mThe shell is a program\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nThe shell reads your line, finds the program you named, and runs it.\r\n", "len": 107}
{"ts": 0.065335, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "It is itself a program, and you can look at it.\r\n\r\n  \u001b[92mecho $BASH_VERSION\u001b[0m     \u001b[90m# the version of the shell running now\u001b[0m\r\n  \u001b[92mps -o pid,comm\u001b[0m         \u001b[90m# the programs on this terminal, by name\u001b[0m\r\n\r\nTwo of those lines are shells: the tutor's own, and the one you are\r\ntyping into. \u001b[92m$BASH_VERSION\u001b[0m is a \u001b[1mvariable\u001b[0m: a name that holds a value.\r\n\r\n\u001b[93m▶ Run both, then type \u001b[92mnext\u001b[93m.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n", "len": 431}
{"ts": 0.068901, "dir": "out", "enc": "utf8", "data": "\u001b[1;90mnext\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(go on)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mshow\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(this screen again)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mprev\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(back)\u001b[0m   \u001b[1;90mquit\u001b[0m \u001b[90m(save and leave)\u001b[0m\r\n", "len": 159}
